  "question": {
    "text": "107. $\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}$ and $\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}$ are two non-collinear unit vectors such that $\\left|\\frac{\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}}{\\mathbf{2}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{u}} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{v}}\\right|=1$. Then the value of $|\\hat{\\mathbf{u}} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{v}}|$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\r\n$\\left|\\frac{\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}}{2}\\right|$\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$|\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}|$\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$|\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}|$\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$\\left|\\frac{\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}}{2}\\right|$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given that, $\\left|\\frac{\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}}{2}+\\hat{\\mathbf{u}} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{v}}\\right|=1$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{ll}\r\n\\Rightarrow & \\left|\\frac{\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}+\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}}{2}+\\hat{\\mathbf{u}} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{v}}\\right|^2=1 \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow & \\frac{2+2 \\cos \\theta}{4}+\\sin ^2 \\theta=1 \\\\\r\n & \\quad[\\because \\hat{\\mathbf{u}} \\cdot(\\hat{\\mathbf{u}} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{v}})=\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}(\\hat{\\mathbf{u}} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{v}})=0] \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow & \\cos ^2 \\frac{\\theta}{2}=\\cos 2 \\theta \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow & \\theta=n \\pi \\pm \\frac{\\theta}{2}, n \\in z \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow & \\theta=\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad|\\hat{\\mathbf{u}} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{v}}|=\\sin \\frac{2 \\pi}{3}=\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{3}=\\left|\\frac{\\hat{\\mathbf{u}}-\\hat{\\mathbf{v}}}{2}\\right|$"
  }
